1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,200
Your viewing history is more than a recommendation signal.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:07,800
It is a path through what held your attention.

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:12,000
WatchTree turns links you choose into a private memory tree.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,500
WatchTree never reads your YouTube account history.

5
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:20,500
You choose every link that enters your private collection.

6
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:27,500
This scene uses verified URL entry only after final Production UAT;
otherwise it stays visibly synthetic.

7
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:36,000
There is no YouTube OAuth, no YouTube API key,
no automatic account access, and no metadata lookup.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:45,500
As the collection grows, WatchTree shows its count,
repeat tendency, time rhythm, and sequence.

9
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:51,500
Every signal comes from records you provided.

10
00:00:51,500 --> 00:01:00,000
It does not invent unsupported metadata
or turn your choices into an AI profile.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:08,500
WatchTree compares the private tree with clearly synthetic
viewing archetypes, never real people.

12
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:14,000
Matching is deterministic and explainable.

13
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,500
You can inspect the evidence behind a result.

14
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:25,000
There is no percentage, no soulmate score,
and no hidden AI ranking.

15
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:31,000
You choose which evidence to reveal and give explicit consent.

16
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:39,000
The result stays visibly labeled: Synthetic archetype.
Simulated mutual. No real user contacted.

17
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:48,000
It is a bounded demonstration of consent,
not a claim that another person was reached.

18
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Privacy continues through the whole lifecycle.

19
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Exclude a record, turn matching off,
or delete everything and return to an empty state.

20
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Deletion is a product feature, not a footer promise.

21
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:15,500
Base44 supplies Auth, owner-scoped Entities and row-level security,
caller-scoped Deno Functions, runtime, hosting, and deployment authority.

22
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:21,500
Current source contains thirteen Entity schemas
and thirteen Function sources.

23
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:28,000
Production proof remains separate from latest source
until deployment and authenticated UAT.

24
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
WatchTree by Resonance. Your memory, your rules.

25
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Built for the Base44 Dev Build-Off.

26
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,000
The verified Production URL is on screen.
